ssions What they control:","• Who approves","• Manipulate workflow","• Editing","Form Request Notifications For requesters and approvers"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p16-img1","page":16},{"ref":"p16-img2","page":16},{"ref":"p16-img3","page":16},{"ref":"p16-img4","page":16},{"ref":"p16-img5","page":16},{"ref":"p16-img6","page":16}]},{"path":"p17","title":"17","level":1,"page":17,"paragraphs":["Configuring eProcurement Workflow","Guided Activity:Guided Activity: Configure Workflow for a Request Template","1. Enable form request notifications on the Customer Base and Approver roles.","2. Review the ADW workflow options of the workflow stream your request will pass through.","3. Define the workflow.","4. Create ADW rules and select approvers.","5. Test the workflow.","What We’ll Discuss in this Lesson:What We’ll Discuss in this Lesson:","How is ePro workflow XML interpreted and set up?","Configuring Workflow XML in eProcurement","Topics :","• Workflow Folders XML","• Workflow Definitions XML","• Adding and Configuring Workflow Steps","Activities: Create a new workflow step to meet this requirement: If the requisition is over the user’s PCard limit designated in their profile, then automatically reject it."],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p17-img1","page":17},{"ref":"p17-img2","page":17},{"ref":"p17-img3","page":17},{"ref":"p17-img4","page":17},{"ref":"p17-img5","page":17},{"ref":"p17-img6","page":17}]},{"path":"p18","title":"18","level":1,"page":18,"paragraphs":["Configuring eProcurement Workflow","Guided Activity:Guided Activity: Add a Workflow Step","Create a new workflow step to meet this requirement: If the requisition is over the user’s PCard limit designated in their profile, then automatically reject it.","1. Add the folder with the reject requisition robot into the Workflow Folder XML file.","2. Add a step into the Workflow Definition XML file that will point to the rule and the robot.","3. Create an ADW rule group.","4. Import the Workflow Definition XML file and address any errors.","5. Create an ADW rule to trigger the step.","6. Test the step for your user.","Explicit Folders: Shared or Internal","The folders being set up through the Import/Export tab are “explicit folders” and will be one of two things:","• Shared folder for manual approvals","• Internal folder for automated actions","Process Files Folder Files"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p18-img1","page":18},{"ref":"p18-img2","page":18},{"ref":"p18-img3","page":18},{"ref":"p18-img4","page":18},{"ref":"p18-img5","page":18},{"ref":"p18-img6","page":18},{"ref":"p18-img7","page":18},{"ref":"p18-img8","page":18},{"ref":"p18-img9","page":18},{"ref":"p18-img10","page":18},{"ref":"p18-img11","page":18},{"ref":"p18-img12","page":18},{"ref":"p18-img13","page":18},{"ref":"p18-img14","page":18}]},{"path":"p19","title":"19","level":1,"page":19,"paragraphs":["Configuring eProcurement Workflow","XML Folders File","• Available to JAGGAER/partner user s with appropriate permissions","• For identifying Shared folders and robots","XML Folders File Folder types:","• Shared","• Automated"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p19-img1","page":19},{"ref":"p19-img2","page":19},{"ref":"p19-img3","page":19},{"ref":"p19-img4","page":19},{"ref":"p19-img5","page":19},{"ref":"p19-img6","page":19},{"ref":"p19-img7","page":19},{"ref":"p19-img8","page":19},{"ref":"p19-img9","page":19},{"ref":"p19-img10","page":19},{"ref":"p19-img11","page":19},{"ref":"p19-img12","page":19}]},{"path":"p20","title":"20","level":1,"page":20,"paragraphs":["Configuring eProcurement Workflow","Guided Activity:Guided Activity: Add a Workflow Step","Create a new workflow step to meet this requirement: If the requisition is over the user’s PCard limit designated in their profile, then automatically reject it.","1. Add the folder with the reject requisition robot into the Workflow Folder XML file.","2. Add a step into the Workflow Definition XML file that will point to the rule and the robot.","3. Create an ADW rule group.","4. Import the Workflow Definition XML file and address any errors.","5. Create an ADW rule to trigger the step.","6. Test the step for your user.","Use your workbook to complete this step in your site","Workflow Process Configuration","• Workflow steps and activities are set up and managed with an XML file called the Workflow Definition file.","• This is uploaded from the Process Configuration tab for each workflow.","• The tab is accessible only to JAGGAER employees and partners.","• Clients cannot update workflow XML."],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p20-img1","page":20},{"ref":"p20-img2","page":20},{"ref":"p20-img3","page":20},{"ref":"p20-img4","page":20},{"ref":"p20-img5","page":20},{"ref":"p20-img6","page":20}]},{"path":"p21","title":"21","level":1,"page":21,"paragraphs":["Configuring eProcurement Workflow","XML Definition File","Workflow Definition XML","There are three sections within the XML file:","• Steps","• Activities","• Activity Relationships"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p21-img1","page":21},{"ref":"p21-img2","page":21},{"ref":"p21-img3","page":21},{"ref":"p21-img4","page":21},{"ref":"p21-img5","page":21},{"ref":"p21-img6","page":21}]},{"path":"p22","title":"22","level":1,"page":22,"paragraphs":["Configuring eProcurement Workflow","Steps: Defining Workflow Steps","The Steps section shows the steps that clients can see on the approvals tab of a document.","Steps: Defining Workflow Steps","The only necessary element is the Step name tag, which will contain the name of the step itself"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p22-img1","page":22},{"ref":"p22-img2","page":22},{"ref":"p22-img3","page":22},{"ref":"p22-img4","page":22},{"ref":"p22-img5","page":22},{"ref":"p22-img6","page":22}]},{"path":"p23","title":"23","level":1,"page":23,"paragraphs":["Configuring eProcurement Workflow","Steps: Adding Help with an Attribute","Add help text to provide users information about the workflow step by using the wfActivityHelp attribute.","<Step name=\"PO Distribution\"> <Attribute name=\"wfActivityHelp\"> <AttrValue lang=\"default\">System step to distribute a Purchase Order.</AttrValue> </Attribute> </Step>","Steps: Workflow Steps with Attributes Example"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p23-img1","page":23},{"ref":"p23-img2","page":23},{"ref":"p23-img3","page":23}]},{"path":"p24","title":"24","level":1,"page":24,"paragraphs":["Configuring eProcurement Workflow","Best Practice:Best Practice: Creating Workflow XML Markup","• Keep the steps and acti vities in the same order.","• Make names as clear as possible and keep them consistent (e.g., for steps and corresponding activities).","• Document with help.","Best Practice:Best Practice: Working with Clients on Workflow XML","• Every client believes their needs are absolutely unique!","• Encourage clients to start with standard steps and activities and revise as needed from there.","• This brings in best practices and streamlines both th e implementation process the client’s workflow process itself."],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p24-img1","page":24},{"ref":"p24-img2","page":24},{"ref":"p24-img3","page":24},{"ref":"p24-img4","page":24},{"ref":"p24-img5","page":24},{"ref":"p24-img6","page":24}]},{"path":"p25","title":"25","level":1,"page":25,"paragraphs":["Configuring eProcurement Workflow","Activities: Where the Action Happens","• The Activities section is the heart of the workflow where the actual pass/fail decision is made.","• Each step (defined in the Steps section) needs at least one Activity associated with it","• You can have multiple Activities take place within one step, but this is not very common.","Elements of an Activity","All activities contain the same basic elements in this order:","• Activity (name)","• ActivityType","• StepRef","• Rule","• FolderSelectionRule","• Attribute ( optional)"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p25-img1","page":25},{"ref":"p25-img2","page":25},{"ref":"p25-img3","page":25},{"ref":"p25-img4","page":25},{"ref":"p25-img5","page":25},{"ref":"p25-img6","page":25}]},{"path":"p26","title":"26","level":1,"page":26,"paragraphs":["Configuring eProcurement Workflow","Elements of an Activity All activities contain the same basic elements in this order:","• Activity (name)","• ActivityType","• StepRef","• FolderRef Name","• Rule","• FolderSelectionRule","• Attribute ( optional)","In static steps only","Activity Name","• Short description of the activity","• Does not have to match the name of the step it is tied to, but usually does","What is the name of the activity?"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p26-img1","page":26},{"ref":"p26-img2","page":26},{"ref":"p26-img3","page":26},{"ref":"p26-img4","page":26},{"ref":"p26-img5","page":26},{"ref":"p26-img6","page":26},{"ref":"p26-img7","page":26},{"ref":"p26-img8","page":26},{"ref":"p26-img9","page":26}]},{"path":"p27","title":"27","level":1,"page":27,"paragraphs":["Configuring eProcurement Workflow Activity Type","• Can be any of the following:","• Manual","• Notification","• Automated","What type of activity is it?","Step Reference","• Links the Activity to a specific step","• Must exactly match the name used in the Steps section","What step does this activity reference?"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p27-img1","page":27},{"ref":"p27-img2","page":27},{"ref":"p27-img3","page":27},{"ref":"p27-img4","page":27},{"ref":"p27-img5","page":27},{"ref":"p27-img6","page":27},{"ref":"p27-img7","page":27},{"ref":"p27-img8","page":27},{"ref":"p27-img9","page":27},{"ref":"p27-img10","page":27},{"ref":"p27-img11","page":27},{"ref":"p27-img12","page":27}]},{"path":"p28","title":"28","level":1,"page":28,"paragraphs":["Configuring eProcurement Workflow Rule","• XML contains the rules or points to the location in th e system where the rules are housed","What is the trigger and the action to be taken?","Rule Syntax <Rule><![CDATA[ Level . Object = “ Value ”]]></Rule> Three elements","• Level : The subject that’s being evaluated","• Object : The characteristic of th e subject being ev